Boxes changes, dated 2026-10-16, add an explicit working-directory argument
to the native Rust exec import and pass Brush's actual working directory
when replacing a process image. The source patches and build recipe are
maintained at https://github.com/minutei-ai/boxes/tree/main/tooling/guest-patches

Brush is Copyright (c) 2024 reuben olinsky, licensed under MIT.
Its unchanged license is included as brush-LICENSE-MIT.

THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt contains cargo-about's selected dependency license
texts, copyright notices and component inventory for cmd-sh, targeting
wasm32-wasip1. Build dependencies are included; development dependencies
are excluded. The Rust standard library's supplied copyright inventory
is retained in Rust-COPYRIGHT-library.html. Additional Rust, wasi-libc,
musl, cloudlibc, musl-fts and LLVM runtime license files accompany it.

The guest uses the dedicated nightly-2026-03-01 Rust toolchain, wasi-sdk 25,
wasi-libc 574b88da481569b65a237cb80daf9a2d5aeaf82d and LLVM runtimes 19.1.5,
with the source patches supplied by the pinned Rivet checkout.

